        "name": "USN-7907-3",
        "description": "Several security issues were discovered in the Linux kernel. An attacker could possibly use these to compromise the system. This update corrects flaws in the following subsystems:   - Cryptographic API;   - ACPI drivers;   - Hardware monitoring drivers;   - InfiniBand drivers;   - Mailbox framework;   - Network drivers;   - AFS file system;   - Ceph distributed file system;   - Network file system (NFS) server daemon;   - NILFS2 file system;   - File systems infrastructure;   - KVM subsystem;   - L3 Master device support module;   - Tracing infrastructure;   - Memory management;   - Appletalk network protocol;   - Netfilter;   - Open vSwitch; (CVE-2021-47385, CVE-2022-49026, CVE-2022-49390, CVE-2024-49935, CVE-2024-49963, CVE-2024-50067, CVE-2024-50095, CVE-2024-50179, CVE-2024-53090, CVE-2024-53112, CVE-2024-53217, CVE-2024-58083, CVE-2025-21715, CVE-2025-21722, CVE-2025-21761, CVE-2025-21791, CVE-2025-21811, CVE-2025-21855, CVE-2025-37958, CVE-2025-38666, CVE-2025-39964, CVE-2025-40018)",
